test/check/error-constants-compare.sumspec:16:14:
   |
16 | Marker = Tag(1)
   |              ^
Tag is an atomic with no base, so 1 doesn't fit it

test/check/error-constants-compare.sumspec:17:7:
   |
17 | Bad = Missing(1)
   |       ^
unknown type Missing; declare it in __atomics or define it

test/check/error-constants-compare.sumspec:19:34:
   |
19 | units :: App => Percent#p // p < Delay -> Percent'
   |                                  ^
cannot compare p (a Percent) with Delay (a Seconds); they are different types

test/check/error-constants-compare.sumspec:20:32:
   |
20 | kind :: App => Count#k // k == Low -> Count'
   |                                ^
cannot compare k (a Count) with Low (a Percent); they are different types

test/check/error-constants-compare.sumspec:21:31:
   |
21 | text :: App => Name#n // n == Low -> Name'
   |                               ^
cannot compare n (a Name) with Low (a Percent); they are different types

test/check/error-constants-compare.sumspec:22:29:
   |
22 | ordtext :: App => Name#n // n < Main -> Name'
   |                             ^
ordering needs a number or an enumeration, but n is a Name (a __text)

test/check/error-constants-compare.sumspec:22:33:
   |
22 | ordtext :: App => Name#n // n < Main -> Name'
   |                                 ^
ordering needs a number or an enumeration, but Main is a Name (a __text)

test/check/error-constants-compare.sumspec:23:32:
   |
23 | ordtag :: App => Tag#t // t == Gps.Fix3D -> Tag'
   |                                ^
cannot compare t (a Tag) with Gps.Fix3D (a Gps); they are different types

test/check/error-constants-compare.sumspec:24:25:
   |
24 | lone :: App => Gps#g // Fix -> Gps'
   |                         ^
Fix is a constant, not a type; it can only be compared in a guard, or be a value in a target

test/check/error-constants-compare.sumspec:25:51:
   |
25 | broken :: App => Percent#p // p < Bad and Off2 == Fix -> Percent'
   |                                                   ^
cannot compare Off2 (a Other) with Fix (a Gps); they are different types

test/check/error-constants-compare.sumspec:29:20:
   |
29 | BadVariant = Shape.Circle
   |                    ^
Shape.Circle has a payload, so it can't be written as a value; test it with a pattern

test/check/error-constants-compare.sumspec:30:18:
   |
30 | BadProduct = App(1)
   |                  ^
App is neither a number, text nor an enumeration, so 1 doesn't fit it

